@meeting train.m5.calder
// Pillar 5, M5 tuning (Day 4, Thursday 10:15, the galley, Oven 1's panel). Calder only in the cast (the training
// meeting waits for its cast; Brennan's words are her own 'work' lines: the breakfast grumble and the biscuit).
// Head writer, seat W.
title: Tuning
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Calder showed you tuning: turn a setting a step at a time and watch the machine answer. Settle it and it's done.
== lines
calder: Brennan's oven runs hot. Forty rolls, burnt edges. She's told everyone.
calder: Nothing's broken. It's drifted. Machines drift.
calder > you: Watch the glow, not the dial.   [gesture]
calder: One step down. Watch. It stutters less. Another. Steady. Done.
calder: Overshoot and it shows the other way. Turn it back. That's all.
? choice
* How far is too far?   rel:calder+2 flavour:practical
  calder: The machine tells you. Dim is too far. Steady is right.   [nod]
* Why do they drift?   rel:calder+1 flavour:listen
  calder: Heat. Use. Time. Same reasons people do.
* (Look at the burnt rolls)
  calder: Brennan's keeping them. As evidence.
calder: Oven 2 is doing the same. Your turn.
